.DS_Store

# Claude Code. Only plans are tracked; everything else under .claude/ is not.
#
# Both settings files stay out. `settings.json` is the *team* file and
# `settings.local.json` the personal one, but this is a one-person repo, so the
# team file has no job -- and approving a permission writes to one of them,
# which would otherwise turn every "don't ask again" into a commit. The rules
# that matter live in ~/.claude/settings.json, and the guard hook with them.
.claude/*
!.claude/plans/
# The guard's rules must stay tracked: the engine exits clean when it finds no
# rules file, so an untracked one would disarm the guard on a fresh clone with
# nothing to show for it. Tracked, its removal at least turns up in a diff.
!.claude/guard-rules.json

# Build output
dist/

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Environment variables
.env
.env.*

# Logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

